 "rulebook": "CrossFit Games movement standard, toes-to-bar: from a full hang with the arms extended and the heels behind the bar, both feet touch the bar at the same time between the hands; kipping is allowed. The bar is the FIG horizontal bar (FIG Apparatus Norms: 2.80 m above the floor, 2.40 m between the uprights, 28 mm in diameter) over 0.20 m mats",
 "deviations": [
  "the grip (no fingers on this robot): each hand's grip is a rigid hold on the bar (the simulator's weld), and the bar turns freely in its bearings about its own axis in place of the hands turning round a fixed bar, because the hands cannot wrap a bar; opening a grip lets go",
  "CrossFit standard (the full hang is judged by eye: arms extended, heels behind the bar): the hang is judged by where the feet are (both feet's centres at least 1.4 m below the bar, nine tenths of the dead hang's 1.55 m, and behind the bar), because the referee has positions, not a judge's eye",
  "FIG Apparatus Norms, horizontal bar (elasticity): the bar is rigid, because the simulator has rigid bodies only"
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Hanging from the high bar by both hands, do five toes-to-bar: bring both feet up to touch the bar between your hands, and come back to the full hang each time, without letting go.",
  "rules": "The bar is 0.028 m thick, 2.8 m above the floor, 2.4 m long between its two uprights, along the y axis; it turns freely about its own axis. Both hands grip it from the start. A repetition has two parts, in this order. The touch: both feet touch the bar at the same moment, each at a point between your two hands (shins, knees or anything else on the bar is not a touch, and does not fail). The hang: afterwards the centres of both feet are at least 1.4 m below the bar and behind it (x less than the bar's; the heels back behind the bar), both at the same moment (in your dead hang they are 1.55 m below it). You succeed when the hang of repetition 5 is reached. Swinging is allowed (a kip is legal), as is bending the knees on the way. You fail the moment either hand no longer grips the bar, any part of you touches the uprights, the mats or the floor, or after 60 s.",
  "venue": "At t = 0 you hang still under the middle of the bar, facing +x: both arms straight up, both grips closed on the bar (hands 0.39 m apart: the palms at y = +0.195 and -0.195 m), legs in the standing posture, your pelvis 0.80 m below the bar, your feet 1.55 m below it and 0.04 m behind it, your soles about 1.25 m above the floor (1.05 m above the 0.20 m mats under the bar). Your feet are 0.24 m apart, each 0.08 m wide. A grip command below 0.5 opens that hand and lets go of the bar. Nothing holds the legs up here: the `stand` action keeps the legs in the stance with a feed-forward meant for standing on the ground; `joints` or `lowcmd` rows drive every joint. The uprights stand at the two ends of the bar, 1.2 m to either side of you.",
  "difficulty": "The bar is 0.80 m above your pelvis and your legs are 0.75 m long: hip flexion alone does not bring the toes to the bar, the trunk has to lean back or swing as well, against shoulders of 25 N m, and the legs have to come all the way down again, five times within the time."
 },
